I know of a few variants on death drop.

1) Dragons:  If you really want that dragon scale and didn't get it
the first time, you can cast or zap turn undead at the corpse and try
again.  (IIRC, there's a 1/20 chance that a resurrected dragon corpse
will leave a hide).  I've used this strategy a few times, most often
at the castle, where you can get a pile of 4 dragon corpses pretty
easily.

2) Trolls:  Once in a while, my upper level characters don't feel like
putting a troll out of its misery, and just beat it down each time it
shows up.  Once in a while, the troll has some new treasure.  (In
order to level up my pet Archon, I locked it in a room with a few
trolls while I polypiled and sacrificed - I didn't notice any
particular treasure when I was done).
 
3) The Riders:  Dangerous, but very profitable.  There's a fancy way
of Rider farming involving boulders, magic missile, and tame jellies
which I will leave as an exercise to the reader (in either planning or
google).
 
4) Pudding Farming:  I've never done this, but it's supposed to be
very effective.  The key is that puddings split when hit by iron
weapons, so you want a way to protect yourself from the puddings and
to hit them without doing much damage.  So in the perfect pudding
farming experience: (1) find an altar, and burn "Elbereth" into a spot
adjacent to it.  (2) Fireproof your armor and rustproof 1 real weapon
and 1 -6 dagger.  (3) Get a stethoscope.  (4) Get a pudding.  (5)
Whack a pudding with the -6 dagger, checking occasionally with the
stethoscope, until you have plenty of them.  (6) Kill a couple with
your real weapon, loot them for treasure, and sacrifice them.  (7) go
to (5)  .

